 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\n# JSON extraction with path fails when arguments are missing\n\n## Description\n\nI've discovered an issue with the `build_extract_json_with_path` function in the parser. When either the JSON expression or the path is missing, the function fails to handle it properly.\n\nConsider the following SQL query:\n\n```sql\nSELECT JSON_EXTRACT('[10, 20, [30, 40]]', NULL)\n```\n\nThis query should either return NULL or handle the error gracefully, but instead it causes unexpected behavior.\n\n## Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Try to extract JSON with a NULL path:\n```sql\nSELECT JSON_EXTRACT('[10, 20, [30, 40]]', NULL)\n```\n\n2. Try to extract JSON with a NULL JSON expression:\n```sql\nSELECT JSON_EXTRACT(NULL, '$[1]')\n```\n\nBoth cases fail to handle the NULL values properly.\n\n## Expected behavior\n\nThe function should handle NULL or missing arguments gracefully, either by returning NULL or by providing a clear error message.\n\n## Actual behavior\n\nThe function attempts to process NULL values as if they were valid arguments, leading to unexpected behavior or errors.\n\nThis issue affects multiple dialects including MySQL and SQLite that use JSON extraction functions.\n</issue>\n",
